description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts, make joinDecisionOutcome append a new entry when every existing entry is already joined, instead of silently dropping the outcome.

Apply exactly one edit.

old_string:
      (entry as Record<string, unknown>).outcome = { ...outcome, joined_at: new Date().toISOString() };
      return;
    }
  }
}

new_string:
      (entry as Record<string, unknown>).outcome = { ...outcome, joined_at: new Date().toISOString() };
      return;
    }
  }
  // Every entry is already joined, so the loop above found nowhere to write and used to fall
  // out of this function having recorded NOTHING. That silent drop is how a LANDING becomes
  // invisible. recordApproachDecision pushes a fresh unjoined entry on every pick, so the
  // ordinary compose path is fine; the mitosis-cutover sweep closes gaps in BULK with no pick,
  // so no unjoined entry exists there and the landed:true write was a no-op every time.
  // Measured 2026-09-04: of 32 store-confirmed-landed gaps carrying approach_decisions, 25 had
  // EVERY decision reading landed:false. Appending records the terminal outcome instead of
  // discarding it, and honours the same 5-entry cap recordApproachDecision applies.
  arr.push({ at: new Date().toISOString(), appended_by: "joinDecisionOutcome", outcome: { ...outcome, joined_at: new Date().toISOString() } });
  while (arr.length > 5) arr.shift();
}

acceptance: joinDecisionOutcome records the outcome in all cases. When an unjoined entry exists the behaviour is unchanged. When none exists a new entry is appended carrying the outcome, and the array is trimmed to at most 5 entries.

